Third-party code included in this repository
============================================
sparkle-project/Sparkle 2.10.1
  https://github.com/sparkle-project/Sparkle
  License: MIT (with the external licenses listed in its LICENSE, reproduced
  in full at the end of this file).
  Used as a binary dependency, not copied into the source tree: the Swift
  package (apps/mac/Package.swift, exact 2.10.1, Package.resolved revision
  ab7d71291238df6e0492143b120c9b696a35f603) links Sparkle.framework into
  OffloadMac only, and Offload.app ships it under Contents/Frameworks. The
  release workflow runs Sparkle's sign_update and generate_appcast from the
  2.10.1 release archive, verified against GitHub's published SHA-256 digest
  (apps/mac/Packaging/fetch-sparkle-tools.sh). Added by slice
  m3-03-mac-signing-sparkle. Offload.app carries this file as
  Contents/Resources/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt.

No third-party source code is copied into this repository yet.

Rule: when a slice ports code from a third-party project, it moves that
project's entry from "Planned" below to this section in the same commit, with
the exact files or functions taken, and keeps the full license text when the
license requires it. See AGENTS.md ("License boundary and notices").

Planned attributions
====================
Each entry says what v2 plans to take, and whether that is code, paraphrased
text, or ideas only. Copyright lines were read from each project's LICENSE or
source headers on 2026-11-14. The old Offload branches that first used them are
listed in docs/MIGRATION.md (section 6).

farzaa/clicky
  https://github.com/farzaa/clicky
  License: MIT. Copyright (c) 2026 Farza
  Planned, code (adapted), for apps/mac:
  - leanring-buddy/CompanionManager.swift: permission rows polled every 1.5 s
    that tick live; the first-run "proof it sees your screen" moment (done in
    Offload with no model call).
  - leanring-buddy/WindowPositionManager.swift: the permission gate (system
    prompt once per launch, then the Settings pane; a confirmed Screen
    Recording grant survives a CGPreflightScreenCaptureAccess false negative;
    Privacy pane deep links; reveal the app in Finder).
  - leanring-buddy/MenuBarPanelManager.swift: the KeyablePanel pattern (a
    non-activating NSPanel that can become key) for the recordings import
    progress panel.
  - leanring-buddy/CompanionScreenCaptureUtility.swift: frames capped at a
    1280 px long edge.
  Full MIT license text: at the end of this file.

